 "check": {
  "describe": "Default: #3882D6 (H 212, S 74, V 84): white text 3.94:1 AA Large, black text 5.33:1 AA. Dragging the hue handle round to the top right (H 40) and the SV handle up and right gives #F2AA18, rgb(242, 170, 24): white 1.99:1 Fail (red meter), black 10.54:1 AAA; both handles sit where the finger left them and the ring handle keeps its hue while the square is dragged. Dragging the SV handle down darkens the colour and flips the grades. 320x568 shrinks the wheel and compacts the swatch; 820x520 moves the panel beside the wheel. Light: a pale page with dark text and the same colour controls; dark: the dark tool look. Mono (dark and light): no colour can be shown, so the ring is drawn as its two edges with R Y G C B M marked, the square as an outlined grid labelled SATURATION and VALUE, the handles as hollow rings, the swatch says to read the values, and the hex, H/S/V, rgb(), ratios, meters and grades stay readable (passing grades as filled pills).",
